Q: touch-transparent LazyColumn A: <p>The most reliable way to make layouts in Compose visible but ignored by the touch system is to use <a href="https://developer.android.com/reference/kotlin/androidx/compose/ui/Modifier#(androidx.compose.ui.Modifier).pointerInteropFilter(androidx.compose.ui.input.pointer.RequestDisallowInterceptTouchEvent,kotlin.Function1)" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><code>pointerInteropFilter</code></a>. By returning <code>false</code>, you tell the underlying Android View system that this component did not handle the touch, prompting it to pass the event to the next view in the stack.</p>
<pre class="lang-kotlin prettyprint-override"><code>LazyColumn(
    modifier = Modifier
        .fillMaxSize()
        .pointerInteropFilter {
            // Returning false tells the system this view 
            // didn't handle the touch. It passes through.
            false 
        },
    userScrollEnabled = false
) {
    items(100) { index -&gt;
        Text(&quot;Ghost Item $index&quot;, modifier = Modifier.padding(16.dp))
    }
}
</code></pre>
